WEBVTT

00:03:58.221 --> 00:04:00.193
AG: Plenty of people are still dissecting

00:04:00.217 --> 00:04:02.360
what happened on the
business side of WeWork.

00:04:02.384 --> 00:04:04.336
I wanted to explore something different,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.712
the leadership and culture.

00:04:05.736 --> 00:04:07.839
We know visions and values
have a real impact

00:04:07.863 --> 00:04:09.919
on whether a company succeed or fail,

00:04:09.943 --> 00:04:12.891
and WeWork was an extreme
example of doing both.

00:04:13.412 --> 00:04:15.737
What could we learn
from WeWork's rise and demise

00:04:15.761 --> 00:04:18.149
about how culture is built and sustained?

00:04:18.173 --> 00:04:20.685
When is a strong culture actually helpful?

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:23.459
And when do you trust
your sense that something is off?

00:04:24.624 --> 00:04:27.384
I can't think of a better person
to ask than Dave.

00:04:27.408 --> 00:04:29.816
He had a front row seat
to the company's evolution,

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.513
expansion and peak.